## Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project.

### Implementation Details

**Framework Identified:** Next.js 16.3.1 (App Router)

**Changes Made:**

1. **Package Installation:**
   - Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package using npm
   - Package version: Latest from npm registry

2. **Configuration (src/app/layout.tsx):**
   - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
   - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout's body, right after the existing `<Analytics />` component
   - This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+ with App Router

3. **Files Modified:**
   - `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights to dependencies
   - `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
   - `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component

### Implementation Approach

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I:
1. Fetched the latest documentation to ensure up-to-date instructions
2. Identified this as a Next.js 16+ project using the App Router
3. Applied the framework-specific configuration for Next.js by adding the SpeedInsights component to the root layout
4. Placed it alongside the existing Analytics component for consistency

### Testing & Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No new linting errors introduced (pre-existing lint errors are unrelated to this change)
✅ Project compiles without TypeScript errors
✅ All routes generated correctly during build

### Deployment Notes

- Speed Insights will automatically activate when the project is deployed to Vercel
- Metrics will become available in the Vercel dashboard after deployment and visitor activity
- The tracking script will be served at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes
- No additional configuration is required

### Package Information

The Speed Insights package monitors Core Web Vitals and performance metrics including:
- First Contentful Paint (FCP)
- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- First Input Delay (FID)
- Time to First Byte (TTFB)
